- op: discuss  # 61e6
  at: '2026-07-28T23:52:16Z'  # 61e6
  by: agent  # 61e6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 61e6
  clock: 4  # 61e6
  nonce: '61e6'  # 61e6
  message: "DONE — PR #57 merged, dev @ 5ed61c45f6 (CI green). ADR-0039 R5 Stage B closed.\n\nDELIVERED: the per-evidence-type base_confidence projection is generated from evidence_types.EVIDENCE_TYPES — 80 of 125 pathways seeded, rendered as a value->pathways table (band 0.40-0.95), plus the 2 is_resolved-conditioned call pathways with both bases, plus the 45 unseeded pathways disclosed explicitly, plus the derived value inline on every evidence-type bullet for point lookup. Freshness gate: 'generate-concept-axes --check', already wired into pre-commit AND verify-generated.\n\nHOMING DECISION (deviates from the item's literal 'into spec §12', follows its named precedent): landed in docs/concept-axes.md, not injected into the spec. Reasons — (a) the item names 'the concept-axes generated-docs pattern' as its model, and that pattern IS a standalone generated doc; (b) concept-axes.md already enumerates all 125 evidence_type values and already carries the --check gate, so the projection inherits enforcement instead of adding a second generator + second gate; (c) injecting machine-generated content into the hand-maintained spec would make every future spec edit a freshness-gate hazard. Spec §12 now owns the MODEL and links the table for the VALUES, so the two cannot drift — which is the item's actual requirement ('deferred rather than hand-transcribing a drift-prone table'). This is the same consolidate-onto-the-existing-home shape as the 7 new-axis reversals.\n\nBONUS FIX (stale prose caught by doing the work): spec §12's 'Bands' paragraph still named build_dependency / subdir_include / tree_sitter as not-yet-derived producers emitting a reserved 1.0. WI-radim (PR #46, pt.38) had already seeded the two meson pathways at 0.95 with literals dropped, and relabelled the jsonnet import edge off the generic 'tree_sitter' mechanism-type onto the already-seeded 'import'. Verified live against the registry while generating the table: build_dependency and subdir_include both render at 0.95; tree_sitter is in the unseeded list. Paragraph rewritten — cohort recorded as CLOSED, the one genuine residual named (jsonnet *calls* edge via a computed variable = WI-rafut), and unseeded pathways now described by their actual contract (derive_confidence returns None -> producer keeps its literal -> confidence_source stays emitter_constant) instead of a fixed three-item list that decays.\n\nTESTS: 7 new (18 total in tests/test_generate_concept_axes.py), incl. a FAITHFULNESS property — every seeded pathway must appear under a table row whose value equals its registry base_confidence — so the table cannot silently diverge even if the renderer is refactored; plus a guard that the shared bullet formatter stays silent for the edge-type / symbol-kind registries, which carry no confidence axis. 0 changed source files under packages/*/src, so no coverage-gate delta; ran the 3 out-of-slice doc-reading test files (248 passed) since the smart-test slice was 1 file."  # 61e6
